h":"/home/admin_/database.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/dependencies.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/cache.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/schemas.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/tasks.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/models.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/ARCHITECTURE.md","language":"markdown","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"CHAT_SUGGESTED_EDIT","isUntitled":true},{"path":"/home/admin_/README-cloudshell.txt","language":"plaintext","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"CHAT_FILE_REFERENCED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/node_modules/googleapis/build/src/apis/cloudtasks/v2.d.ts","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/google/adk/agents/parallel_agent.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/uvicorn/protocols/http/h11_impl.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/node_modules/googleapis/build/src/apis/cloudtasks/v2beta3.d.ts","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/node_modules/googleapis/build/src/apis/cloudtasks/v2beta2.d.ts","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/node_modules/require-directory/README.markdown","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/node_modules/resolve/readme.markdown","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/node_modules/buffer-equal-constant-time/LICENSE.txt","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/google/adk/agents/config_schemas/AgentConfig.json","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false}],"rules":null,"editableRegion":null,"recentUserActions":null,"chatSectionId":"3"},"id":"5b2f3528-89aa-4a5d-a2c1-558eea3aaae7","agentMetadata":{"coderAgent":{"kind":""},"model":""}},{"traceId":"b76011a7fc542b5c","entity":"SYSTEM","markdownText":"To continue the implementation of the **Shtiya OS** core according to the master blueprint, we will now focus on **Deliverable 3 (Containerization)** and **Deliverable 4 (The Deep Build Manual)**.\n\nThese steps transition the secure Python code into a production-ready, HIPAA-compliant execution unit on Google Cloud Run. The container strategy focuses on a minimized attack surface using multi-stage builds and non-root execution, while the deployment manual leverages **Direct VPC Egress** to maintain Zero-Trust connectivity without the performance bottlenecks of legacy VPC connectors.\n\nHere are the operational files and the deployment manual.\n\n### Deliverable 3: Containerization\n\n```diff\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/home/admin_/Dockerfile\n@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@\n+# Dockerfile\n+# ==============================================================================\n+# SHTIYA OS: NODE 01 - ASSURED WORKLOADS RUNTIME ENVIRONMENT\n+# ==============================================================================\n+\n+# 1. Base Image: Leverage slim Python for minimized attack surface\n+FROM python:3.11-slim as builder\n+\n+# 2. Prevent Python from buffering standard output and writing bytecode\n+ENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \\\n+    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1\n+\n+# 3. System dependencies for pg8000 and cryptography compilation\n+RUN apt-get update \u0026\u0026 apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\\n+    gcc \\\n+    libpq-dev \\\n+    \u0026\u0026 rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\n+\n+WORKDIR /app\n+\n+# 4. Dependency caching layer\n+COPY requirements.txt .\n+# Compile wheels locally to accelerate the final stage image creation\n+RUN pip install --no-cache-dir --upgrade pip \u0026\u0026 \\\n+    pip wheel --no-cache-dir --no-deps --wheel-dir /app/wheels -r requirements.txt\n+\n+# 5. Final Stage Execution\n+FROM python:3.11-slim\n+\n+ENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \\\n+    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1\n+\n+# Establish a non-root user to satisfy strict Assured Workloads security policies\n+RUN groupadd -r shtiya_group \u0026\u0026 useradd -r -g shtiya_group shtiya_user\n+\n+WORKDIR /app\n+\n+# Copy compiled wheels from builder and install them cleanly\n+COPY --from=builder /app/wheels /wheels\n+COPY --from=builder /app/requirements.txt .\n+RUN pip install --no-cache /wheels/*\n+\n+# 6. Establish application payload\n+COPY . /app/\n+\n+# Transfer ownership of the execution directory to the non-root user\n+RUN chown -R shtiya_user:shtiya_group /app\n+\n+# Drop privileges\n+USER shtiya_user\n+\n+# 7. Expose default Cloud Run port and launch via Uvicorn\n+EXPOSE 8080\n+\n+CMD [\"uvicorn\", \"main:app\", \"--host\", \"0.0.0.0\", \"--port\", \"8080\", \"--workers\", \"4\", \"--proxy-headers\"]\n```\n\n```diff\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/home/admin_/requirements.txt\n@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@\n+# Web Framework \u0026 Validation\n+fastapi==0.111.0\n+uvicorn[standard]==0.30.1\n+pydantic==2.7.4\n+\n+# Database Subsystem \u0026 GCP Connectors\n+sqlalchemy==2.0.30\n+pgvector==0.3.0\n+google-cloud-sql-connector[pg8000]==1.5.0\n+alembic==1.13.1\n+\n+# Caching \u0026 Queue Subsystem\n+redis==5.0.4\n+celery==5.4.0\n+\n+# Security \u0026 Compliance\n+cryptography==42.0.8\n+google-auth==2.29.0\n```\n\n### Deliverable 4: The Deep Build Manual\n\n```diff\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/home/admin_/deployment.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@\n+# Shtiya OS: Node 01 Deployment Manual (Compute Core)\n+\n+This manual outlines the exact steps to deploy the containerized Node 01 architecture into the GCP Assured Workloads environment using **Direct VPC Egress**.\n+\n+## Step 1: Provision the Assured Workloads Artifact Registry\n+Docker images must reside strictly within the designated regulatory boundary.\n+\n+```bash\n+gcloud artifacts repositories create shtiya-os-registry \\\n+    --repository-format=docker \\\n+    --location=us-central1 \\\n+    --description=\"HIPAA-compliant Docker registry for Shtiya OS Node 01\" \\\n+    --project=shtiya-os-assured-workloads\n+```\n+\n+## Step 2: Build and Push the Container\n+Using Google Cloud Build ensures the compilation process remains internal.\n+\n+```bash\n+gcloud builds submit \\\n+    --tag us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/shtiya-os-assured-workloads/shtiya-os-registry/node-01:v1.8.4 \\\n+    --project=shtiya-os-assured-workloads\n+```\n+\n+## Step 3: Identity and Access Management (IAM) Configuration\n+The principle of least privilege is absolute. The Cloud Run service requires a dedicated Service Account.\n+\n+```bash\n+# 3.1 Create the strict service account\n+gcloud iam service-accounts create node-01-sa \\\n+    --display-name=\"Node 01 Application Core Identity\" \\\n+    --project=shtiya-os-assured-workloads\n+\n+# 3.2 Grant Cloud SQL Client Role \n+gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding shtiya-os-assured-workloads \\\n+    --member=\"serviceAccount:node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam.gserviceaccount.com\" \\\n+    --role=\"roles/cloudsql.client\"\n+\n+# 3.3 Grant Cloud SQL Instance User Role \n+gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding shtiya-os-assured-workloads \\\n+    --member=\"serviceAccount:node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam.gserviceaccount.com\" \\\n+    --role=\"roles/cloudsql.instanceUser\"\n+\n+# 3.4 Grant Vertex AI User Role\n+gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding shtiya-os-assured-workloads \\\n+    --member=\"serviceAccount:node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam.gserviceaccount.com\" \\\n+    --role=\"roles/aiplatform.user\"\n+```\n+\n+## Step 4: The Direct VPC Egress Cloud Run Deployment\n+Crucially, the flag `--vpc-egress=private-ranges-only` forces the container to route traffic mapped to internal CIDR blocks directly through the internal VPC.\n+\n+```bash\n+gcloud run deploy node-01-core \\\n+    --image us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/shtiya-os-assured-workloads/shtiya-os-registry/node-01:v1.8.4 \\\n+    --region=us-central1 \\\n+    --project=shtiya-os-assured-workloads \\\n+    --service-account=node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam.gserviceaccount.com \\\n+    --network=shtiya-vpc \\\n+    --subnet=shtiya-private-subnet \\\n+    --vpc-egress=private-ranges-only \\\n+    --allow-unauthenticated \\\n+    --set-env-vars=\"INSTANCE_CONNECTION_NAME=shtiya-os-assured-workloads:us-central1:shtiya-db-05,DB_IAM_USER=node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam,REDIS_HOST=10.0.0.5\" \\\n+    --min-instances=3 \\\n+    --max-instances=50\n+```\n+\n+## Step 5: Database Privileges Initialization\n+Grant Data Manipulation Language (DML) rights strictly to the application identity inside Node 05.\n+\n+```sql\n+-- Connect to Postgres as superuser and execute:\n+GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA public TO \"node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam\";\n+GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON tenants, users, matters, case_embeddings, medical_chronologies TO \"node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam\";\n+```\n```\n\nWith these artifacts, the transition from code to a hardened, deployed cloud environment is fully planned. We have addressed the container security requirements and the network egress logic defined in **ArchitectureII.md**.\n\n\u003c!--\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]Can you help me write the SQL commands to enable pgvector and set up the RLS policies in the Cloud SQL instance?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]How can we implement the Vertex AI embedding logic within the Celery worker task in tasks.py?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n--\u003e","chatSectionId":"3","promptCitations":[{"startIndex":757,"endIndex":2579,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","citationText":"Dockerfile\n+# ==============================================================================\n+# SHTIYA OS: NODE 01 - ASSURED WORKLOADS RUNTIME ENVIRONMENT\n+# ==============================================================================\n+\n+# 1. Base Image: Leverage slim Python for minimized attack surface\n+FROM python:3.11-slim as builder\n+\n+# 2. Prevent Python from buffering standard output and writing bytecode\n+ENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \\\n+    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1\n+\n+# 3. System dependencies for pg8000 and cryptography compilation\n+RUN apt-get update \u0026\u0026 apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\\n+    gcc \\\n+    libpq-dev \\\n+    \u0026\u0026 rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\n+\n+WORKDIR /app\n+\n+# 4. Dependency caching layer\n+COPY requirements.txt .\n+# Compile wheels locally to accelerate the final stage image creation\n+RUN pip install --no-cache-dir --upgrade pip \u0026\u0026 \\\n+    pip wheel --no-cache-dir --no-deps --wheel-dir /app/wheels -r requirements.txt\n+\n+# 5. Final Stage Execution\n+FROM python:3.11-slim\n+\n+ENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \\\n+    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1\n+\n+# Establish a non-root user to satisfy strict Assured Workloads security policies\n+RUN groupadd -r shtiya_group \u0026\u0026 useradd -r -g shtiya_group shtiya_user\n+\n+WORKDIR /app\n+\n+# Copy compiled wheels from builder and install them cleanly\n+COPY --from=builder /app/wheels /wheels\n+COPY --from=builder /app/requirements.txt .\n+RUN pip install --no-cache /wheels/*\n+\n+# 6. Establish application payload\n+COPY . /app/\n+\n+# Transfer ownership of the execution directory to the non-root user\n+RUN chown -R shtiya_user:shtiya_group /app\n+\n+# Drop privileges\n+USER shtiya_user\n+\n+# 7. Expose default Cloud Run port and launch via Uvicorn\n+EXPOSE 8080\n+\n+CMD [\"uvicorn\", \"main:app\", \"--host\", \"0.0.0.0\", \"--port\", \"8080\", \"--workers\", \"4\", \"--proxy-headers\"]\n```\n\n```","isUntitled":false},{"startIndex":2653,"endIndex":2729,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","citationText":"Web Framework \u0026 Validation\n+fastapi==0.111.0\n+uvicorn[standard]==0.30.1\n+pyd","isUntitled":false},{"startIndex":3233,"endIndex":3315,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","citationText":"the containerized Node 01 architecture into the GCP Assured Workloads environment ","isUntitled":false},{"startIndex":3350,"endIndex":3480,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","citationText":"Step 1: Provision the Assured Workloads Artifact Registry\n+Docker images must reside strictly within the designated regulatory bou","isUntitled":false},{"startIndex":3493,"endIndex":3860,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","citationText":"bash\n+gcloud artifacts repositories create shtiya-os-registry \\\n+    --repository-format=docker \\\n+    --location=us-central1 \\\n+    --description=\"HIPAA-compliant Docker registry for Shtiya OS Node 01\" \\\n+    --project=shtiya-os-assured-workloads\n+```\n+\n+## Step 2: Build and Push the Container\n+Using Google Cloud Build ensures the compilation process remains inter","isUntitled":false},{"startIndex":3871,"endIndex":4217,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","citationText":"bash\n+gcloud builds submit \\\n+    --tag us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/shtiya-os-assured-workloads/shtiya-os-registry/node-01:v1.8.4 \\\n+    --project=shtiya-os-assured-workloads\n+```\n+\n+## Step 3: Identity and Access Management (IAM) Configuration\n+The principle of least privilege is absolute. The Cloud Run service requires a dedicated Service Acco","isUntitled":false},{"startIndex":4228,"endIndex":5214,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","citationText":"bash\n+# 3.1 Create the strict service account\n+gcloud iam service-accounts create node-01-sa \\\n+    --display-name=\"Node 01 Application Core Identity\" \\\n+    --project=shtiya-os-assured-workloads\n+\n+# 3.2 Grant Cloud SQL Client Role \n+gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding shtiya-os-assured-workloads \\\n+    --member=\"serviceAccount:node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam.gserviceaccount.com\" \\\n+    --role=\"roles/cloudsql.client\"\n+\n+# 3.3 Grant Cloud SQL Instance User Role \n+gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding shtiya-os-assured-workloads \\\n+    --member=\"serviceAccount:node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam.gserviceaccount.com\" \\\n+    --role=\"roles/cloudsql.instanceUser\"\n+\n+# 3.4 Grant Vertex AI User Role\n+gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding shtiya-os-assured-workloads \\\n+    --member=\"serviceAccount:node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam.gserviceaccount.com\" \\\n+    --role=\"roles/aiplatform.user\"\n+```\n+\n+## Step 4: The Direct VPC Egress Cloud Run Deploymen","isUntitled":false},{"startIndex":5217,"endIndex":5374,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","citationText":"Crucially, the flag `--vpc-egress=private-ranges-only` forces the container to route traffic mapped to internal CIDR blocks directly through the internal VPC","isUntitled":false},{"startIndex":5382,"endIndex":6096,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","citationText":"bash\n+gcloud run deploy node-01-core \\\n+    --image us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/shtiya-os-assured-workloads/shtiya-os-registry/node-01:v1.8.4 \\\n+    --region=us-central1 \\\n+    --project=shtiya-os-assured-workloads \\\n+    --service-account=node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam.gserviceaccount.com \\\n+    --network=shtiya-vpc \\\n+    --subnet=shtiya-private-subnet \\\n+    --vpc-egress=private-ranges-only \\\n+    --allow-unauthenticated \\\n+    --set-env-vars=\"INSTANCE_CONNECTION_NAME=shtiya-os-assured-workloads:us-central1:shtiya-db-05,DB_IAM_USER=node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam,REDIS_HOST=10.0.0.5\" \\\n+    --min-instances=3 \\\n+    --max-instances=50\n+```\n+\n+## Step 5: Database Privileges Initiali","isUntitled":false},{"startIndex":6104,"endIndex":6181,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","citationText":"Grant Data Manipulation Language (DML) rights strictly to the application ide","isUntitled":false},{"startIndex":6209,"endIndex":6490,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","citationText":"sql\n+-- Connect to Postgres as superuser and execute:\n+GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA public TO \"node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam\";\n+GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON tenants, users, matters, case_embeddings, medical_chronologies TO \"node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.i","isUntitled":false}],"ideContext":{"currentFile":{"path":"/home/admin_/main.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"CURRENTLY_OPEN","isUntitled":false},"remoteContexts":null,"remoteRepositories":[],"otherFiles":[{"path":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","language":"markdown","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/database.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/dependencies.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/cache.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/schemas.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/tasks.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/models.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/ARCHITECTURE.md","language":"markdown","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"CHAT_SUGGESTED_EDIT","isUntitled":true},{"path":"/home/admin_/README-cloudshell.txt","language":"plaintext","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"CHAT_FILE_REFERENCED","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/node_modules/googleapis/build/src/apis/cloudtasks/v2.d.ts","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/google/adk/agents/parallel_agent.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/uvicorn/protocols/http/h11_impl.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/node_modules/googleapis/build/src/apis/cloudtasks/v2beta3.d.ts","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/node_modules/googleapis/build/src/apis/cloudtasks/v2beta2.d.ts","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/node_modules/require-directory/README.markdown","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/node_modules/resolve/readme.markdown","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/node_modules/buffer-equal-constant-time/LICENSE.txt","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false},{"path":"/home/admin_/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/google/adk/agents/config_schemas/AgentConfig.json","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE","isUntitled":false}],"rules":null,"editableRegion":null,"recentUserActions":null,"chatSectionId":"3"},"openFileUri":"file:///home/admin_/main.py","ragStatus":"RAG_NOT_FOUND","timeToFirstToken":"3695","agentProcessingDetails":{},"workspaceChange":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/admin_/Dockerfile","newText":"# Dockerfile\n# ==============================================================================\n# SHTIYA OS: NODE 01 - ASSURED WORKLOADS RUNTIME ENVIRONMENT\n# ==============================================================================\n\n# 1. Base Image: Leverage slim Python for minimized attack surface\nFROM python:3.11-slim as builder\n\n# 2. Prevent Python from buffering standard output and writing bytecode\nENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \\\n    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1\n\n# 3. System dependencies for pg8000 and cryptography compilation\nRUN apt-get update \u0026\u0026 apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\\n    gcc \\\n    libpq-dev \\\n    \u0026\u0026 rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\n\nWORKDIR /app\n\n# 4. Dependency caching layer\nCOPY requirements.txt .\n# Compile wheels locally to accelerate the final stage image creation\nRUN pip install --no-cache-dir --upgrade pip \u0026\u0026 \\\n    pip wheel --no-cache-dir --no-deps --wheel-dir /app/wheels -r requirements.txt\n\n# 5. Final Stage Execution\nFROM python:3.11-slim\n\nENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \\\n    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1\n\n# Establish a non-root user to satisfy strict Assured Workloads security policies\nRUN groupadd -r shtiya_group \u0026\u0026 useradd -r -g shtiya_group shtiya_user\n\nWORKDIR /app\n\n# Copy compiled wheels from builder and install them cleanly\nCOPY --from=builder /app/wheels /wheels\nCOPY --from=builder /app/requirements.txt .\nRUN pip install --no-cache /wheels/*\n\n# 6. Establish application payload\nCOPY . /app/\n\n# Transfer ownership of the execution directory to the non-root user\nRUN chown -R shtiya_user:shtiya_group /app\n\n# Drop privileges\nUSER shtiya_user\n\n# 7. Expose default Cloud Run port and launch via Uvicorn\nEXPOSE 8080\n\nCMD [\"uvicorn\", \"main:app\", \"--host\", \"0.0.0.0\", \"--port\", \"8080\", \"--workers\", \"4\", \"--proxy-headers\"]","promptCitations":[{"startIndex":2,"endIndex":1761,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md"}],"telemetry":{"CommentLines":null},"codeBlockIndex":0,"language":"dockerfile","checkpointFileNotFound":true,"accepted":true},{"filePath":"/home/admin_/requirements.txt","newText":"# Web Framework \u0026 Validation\nfastapi==0.111.0\nuvicorn[standard]==0.30.1\npydantic==2.7.4\n\n# Database Subsystem \u0026 GCP Connectors\nsqlalchemy==2.0.30\npgvector==0.3.0\ngoogle-cloud-sql-connector[pg8000]==1.5.0\nalembic==1.13.1\n\n# Caching \u0026 Queue Subsystem\nredis==5.0.4\ncelery==5.4.0\n\n# Security \u0026 Compliance\ncryptography==42.0.8\ngoogle-auth==2.29.0","promptCitations":[{"startIndex":2,"endIndex":75,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md"}],"telemetry":{"CommentLines":null},"codeBlockIndex":1,"language":"pip requirements","checkpointFileNotFound":true,"accepted":true},{"filePath":"/home/admin_/deployment.md","newText":"# Shtiya OS: Node 01 Deployment Manual (Compute Core)\n\nThis manual outlines the exact steps to deploy the containerized Node 01 architecture into the GCP Assured Workloads environment using **Direct VPC Egress**.\n\n## Step 1: Provision the Assured Workloads Artifact Registry\nDocker images must reside strictly within the designated regulatory boundary.\n\n```bash\ngcloud artifacts repositories create shtiya-os-registry \\\n    --repository-format=docker \\\n    --location=us-central1 \\\n    --description=\"HIPAA-compliant Docker registry for Shtiya OS Node 01\" \\\n    --project=shtiya-os-assured-workloads\n```\n\n## Step 2: Build and Push the Container\nUsing Google Cloud Build ensures the compilation process remains internal.\n\n```bash\ngcloud builds submit \\\n    --tag us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/shtiya-os-assured-workloads/shtiya-os-registry/node-01:v1.8.4 \\\n    --project=shtiya-os-assured-workloads\n```\n\n## Step 3: Identity and Access Management (IAM) Configuration\nThe principle of least privilege is absolute. The Cloud Run service requires a dedicated Service Account.\n\n```bash\n# 3.1 Create the strict service account\ngcloud iam service-accounts create node-01-sa \\\n    --display-name=\"Node 01 Application Core Identity\" \\\n    --project=shtiya-os-assured-workloads\n\n# 3.2 Grant Cloud SQL Client Role \ngcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding shtiya-os-assured-workloads \\\n    --member=\"serviceAccount:node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam.gserviceaccount.com\" \\\n    --role=\"roles/cloudsql.client\"\n\n# 3.3 Grant Cloud SQL Instance User Role \ngcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding shtiya-os-assured-workloads \\\n    --member=\"serviceAccount:node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam.gserviceaccount.com\" \\\n    --role=\"roles/cloudsql.instanceUser\"\n\n# 3.4 Grant Vertex AI User Role\ngcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding shtiya-os-assured-workloads \\\n    --member=\"serviceAccount:node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam.gserviceaccount.com\" \\\n    --role=\"roles/aiplatform.user\"\n```\n\n## Step 4: The Direct VPC Egress Cloud Run Deployment\nCrucially, the flag `--vpc-egress=private-ranges-only` forces the container to route traffic mapped to internal CIDR blocks directly through the internal VPC.\n\n```bash\ngcloud run deploy node-01-core \\\n    --image us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/shtiya-os-assured-workloads/shtiya-os-registry/node-01:v1.8.4 \\\n    --region=us-central1 \\\n    --project=shtiya-os-assured-workloads \\\n    --service-account=node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam.gserviceaccount.com \\\n    --network=shtiya-vpc \\\n    --subnet=shtiya-private-subnet \\\n    --vpc-egress=private-ranges-only \\\n    --allow-unauthenticated \\\n    --set-env-vars=\"INSTANCE_CONNECTION_NAME=shtiya-os-assured-workloads:us-central1:shtiya-db-05,DB_IAM_USER=node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam,REDIS_HOST=10.0.0.5\" \\\n    --min-instances=3 \\\n    --max-instances=50\n```\n\n## Step 5: Database Privileges Initialization\nGrant Data Manipulation Language (DML) rights strictly to the application identity inside Node 05.\n\n```sql\n-- Connect to Postgres as superuser and execute:\nGRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA public TO \"node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam\";\nGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON tenants, users, matters, case_embeddings, medical_chronologies TO \"node-01-sa@shtiya-os-assured-workloads.iam\";\n```","promptCitations":[{"startIndex":102,"endIndex":183,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md"},{"startIndex":217,"endIndex":346,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md"},{"startIndex":357,"endIndex":715,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md"},{"startIndex":724,"endIndex":1063,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md"},{"startIndex":1072,"endIndex":2036,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md"},{"startIndex":2038,"endIndex":2195,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md"},{"startIndex":2201,"endIndex":2900,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md"},{"startIndex":2907,"endIndex":2984,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md"},{"startIndex":3010,"endIndex":3288,"filepath":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md"}],"telemetry":{"CommentLines":null},"codeBlockIndex":2,"language":"markdown","checkpointFileNotFound":true,"accepted":true}]},"fileUsage":{"includedFiles":["/home/admin_/main.py","/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","/home/admin_/database.py","/home/admin_/dependencies.py","/home/admin_/cache.py","/home/admin_/schemas.py","/home/admin_/tasks.py","/home/admin_/models.py","/home/admin_/ARCHITECTURE.md","/home/admin_/README-cloudshell.txt","/home/admin_/node_modules/googleapis/build/src/apis/cloudtasks/v2.d.ts","/home/admin_/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/google/adk/agents/parallel_agent.py","/home/admin_/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/uvicorn/protocols/http/h11_impl.py","/home/admin_/node_modules/googleapis/build/src/apis/cloudtasks/v2beta3.d.ts","/home/admin_/node_modules/googleapis/build/src/apis/cloudtasks/v2beta2.d.ts","/home/admin_/node_modules/require-directory/README.markdown","/home/admin_/node_modules/resolve/readme.markdown","/home/admin_/node_modules/buffer-equal-constant-time/LICENSE.txt","/home/admin_/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/google/adk/agents/config_schemas/AgentConfig.json"]},"suggestedPrompts":["Can you help me write the SQL commands to enable pgvector and set up the RLS policies in the Cloud SQL instance?","How can we implement the Vertex AI embedding logic within the Celery worker task in tasks.py?"],"thinkingSummaryMarkdownText":"**Building Secure Core**\n\nI'm focusing on establishing the secure application core as outlined in the \"Shtiya OS Master Architecture\" document, particularly `ArchitecureII.md`. My goal is to lay a robust foundation for our development efforts.\n\n**Planning Next Steps**\n\nWith the core models and application code confirmed, my focus now shifts to containerizing the application and drafting the deep build manual. I'm outlining the `Dockerfile` structure, including multi-stage builds and a non-root user, and preparing the necessary `requirements.txt` for our dependencies. The manual will detail provisioning Artifact Registry and the build and push process using Cloud Build.\n\n**Configuring Cloud Infrastructure**\n\nI'm now detailing the IAM configurations, specifically the creation of service accounts and assigning them necessary roles like `cloudsql.client` and `aiplatform.user`. My current efforts are concentrated on finalizing the `Dockerfile`, `requirements.txt`, and the deployment markdown, ensuring they align with the master architecture.\n\n","id":"bb97fb35-71be-4ee1-8938-a17f5380cad3","agentMetadata":{"coderAgent":{"kind":""},"model":""},"modelDisplayName":"3 Flash Preview","modelID":"chat-gemini-3-0-flash-p