ollowing components:\n\n*   **`models.py` \u0026 `schemas.py`**: I followed the \"Cryptographic Database Schemas\" section to implement the 1536-dimensional `pgvector` storage and the Pydantic validation rules.\n*   **`database.py`**: I implemented the Zero-Trust Cloud SQL connection using the `google-cloud-sql-connector` and the `SET LOCAL` Row-Level Security (RLS) injection as dictated by the blueprint.\n*   **`cache.py` \u0026 `tasks.py`**: I configured the Redis TLS and Celery broker settings to match the specific security and connectivity requirements for Node 02/09.\n*   **`dependencies.py`**: I implemented the sliding-window rate limiter using the exact Lua script provided in the architecture to prevent API exhaustion.\n\nRegarding **`ArchitectureI.md`**, that specific file name was not present in the environment I analyzed. However, I did review the high-level **`ARCHITECTURE.md`**, though **`ArchitecureII.md`** provided the deep technical specifications required for the actual implementation of Node 01.\n\nIf there is an `ArchitectureI.md` you'd like me to incorporate, please feel free to drop it into the environment!\n\n\u003c!--\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]Can you review main.py to ensure it strictly follows the CORS and health check requirements in ArchitecureII.md?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]Should we add the Row-Level Security (RLS) SQL setup commands to the ARCHITECTURE.md file for documentation?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n--\u003e","chatSectionId":"2","ideContext":{"currentFile":{"path":"/home/admin_/main.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"CURRENTLY_OPEN"},"remoteContexts":null,"remoteRepositories":[],"otherFiles":[{"path":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","language":"markdown","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED"},{"path":"/home/admin_/database.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED"},{"path":"/home/admin_/dependencies.py","language":