:null,"recentUserActions":null,"chatSectionId":"4"},"id":"03da6d68-0250-4033-adae-3bf43f0afd08","agentMetadata":{"coderAgent":{"kind":""},"model":""}},{"traceId":"2bbd764ad18daea3","entity":"SYSTEM","markdownText":"To push your project from Google Cloud Shell to GitHub, you'll need to initialize a Git repository, handle authentication, and then push your files. Since your code currently only resides in the persistent `/home/admin_` directory of Cloud Shell, this is the standard way to ensure it is backed up and version-controlled.\n\nBefore you start, it is critical to add a `.gitignore` file. This prevents system files, Python cache, and the large `node_modules` folder seen in your environment from being uploaded to GitHub.\n\n### 1. Create a `.gitignore` file\n\n```diff\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/home/admin_/.gitignore\n@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@\n+# Python\n+__pycache__/\n+*.py[cod]\n+*$py.class\n+.venv/\n+venv/\n+\n+# Node/Environment\n+node_modules/\n+.env\n+\n+# System/IDE\n+.DS_Store\n+.idea/\n+.vscode/\n+\n+# GCP specific\n+cloudshell_open/\n```\n\n### 2. Initialize and Commit Locally\nRun these commands in your Cloud Shell terminal:\n\n```bash\n# Initialize the repository\ngit init\n\n# Configure your identity (if you haven't)\ngit config --global user.email \"you@example.com\"\ngit config --global user.name \"Your Name\"\n\n# Stage all files\ngit add .\n\n# Create the initial commit\ngit commit -m \"feat: establish Shtiya OS core architecture and secure compute layer\"\n```\n\n### 3. Create a Repository and Push\nThe most efficient way to do this within Cloud Shell is using the GitHub CLI (`gh`), which is pre-installed.\n\n1.  **Authenticate:** Run `gh auth login` and follow the prompts (choose GitHub.com, HTTPS, and log in via your browser or a token).\n2.  **Create the Remote:**\n    ```bash\n    # This creates a PRIVATE repository on your GitHub account named 'shtiya-os'\n    gh repo create shtiya-os --private --source=. --remote=origin\n    ```\n3.  **Push the Code:**\n    ```bash\n    # Rename your branch to main and push\n    git branch -M main\n    git push -u origin main\n    ```\n\n### Important Security Note\nSince this project involves **HIPAA-compliant** and **Military-Grade** specifications as outlined in `ArchitecureII.md`, ensure the GitHub repository is set to **Private**. Do not include any `.json` service account keys or actual secret values in your files before pushing; ensure you continue to rely on the environment variables defined in your `deployment.md`.\n\n\u003c!--\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]How can I set up a GitHub Action to automatically run the health check from main.py on every push?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]Can you help me create a README.md for the root directory that summarizes the Node 01 features?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n--\u003e","chatSectionId":"4","ideContext":{"currentFile":{"path":"/home/admin_/schemas.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"CURRENTLY_OPEN"},"remoteContexts":null,"remoteRepositories":[],"otherFiles":[{"path":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","language":"markdown","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED"},{"path":"/home/admin_/models.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED"},{"path":"/home/admin_/database.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED"},{"path":"/home/admin_/dependencies.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED"},{"path":"/home/admin_/main.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED"},{"path":"/home/admin_/tasks.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED"},{"path":"/home/admin_/cache.py","language":"python","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED"},{"path":"/home/admin_/Dockerfile","language":"dockerfile","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"incl