 `gopath/` to your ignore list to clean up the repository.\n\n```diff\n--- a/home/admin_/.gitignore\n+++ b/home/admin_/.gitignore\n@@ -16,3 +16,7 @@\n \n # GCP specific\n cloudshell_open/\n+\n+# AI Assistant \u0026 Cloud Shell environment artifacts\n+.gemini/\n+gopath/\n```\n\n### 2. Clear and Re-add your files\n\nSince you have already run `git add .`, the files Git warned about are currently \"staged\" in a way that creates the nested repository issue. Run the following commands in your terminal to fix the state:\n\n```bash\n# Unstage all files to start fresh with the new .gitignore rules\ngit rm -r --cached .\n\n# Re-add all files (it will now respect the updated .gitignore)\ngit add .\n\n# Verify that the .gemini folders are no longer being tracked\ngit status\n```\n\n### 3. Commit your clean codebase\n\nOnce the warnings are gone and `git status` looks correct (showing only your source code, models, and deployment docs), you can proceed with the commit:\n\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"feat: initial commit of Shtiya OS core with secure GCP architecture\"\n```\n\nAfter this, you can proceed with `gh auth login` and `gh repo create` as we planned to get this pushed to a private GitHub repository.\n\n\u003c!--\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]How do I check if my .gitignore is correctly excluding all PHI/PII data files?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]Show me the command to push this local repository to a new private GitHub repo using the 'gh' CLI.[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n--\u003e","chatSectionId":"5","ideContext":{"currentFile":{"path":"/home/admin_/.gitignore","language":"ignore","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"CURRENTLY_OPEN"},"remoteContexts":null,"remoteRepositories":[],"otherFiles":[{"path":"/home/admin_/ArchitecureII.md","language":"markdown","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RECENTLY_EDITED"},{"path":"/home/admin_/Dockerfile","language":"dockerfile","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"CHAT_SUGGESTED_EDIT"},{"path":"/home/