g on resolving the nested `.git` repository warnings. My updated `.gitignore` will now explicitly exclude the `.gemini/` directory. To implement this, I'll then clear the existing Git index and re-add all project files to ensure proper tracking.\n\n**Excluding Tool-Specific Files**\n\nI'm refining the `.gitignore` to exclude `.gemini/` recursively, which should resolve the nested repository warnings. I'm also considering excluding `gopath/` as it appears to be a system artifact and not intended for version control.\n\n","agentMetadata":{"coderAgent":{"kind":""},"model":""},"modelDisplayName":"3 Flash Preview","modelID":"chat-gemini-3-0-flash-preview-free-tier","usageMetadata":{"promptTokenCount":93718,"candidatesTokenCount":505,"totalTokenCount":94223},"id":"4b245600-b479-4df7-8246-369e8a9753fc"}]}
